---
const questions = [
  {
    q: "Can every reported benchmark number carry its own identified range?",
    text: "The benchmark papers show that what is unknown about a scorer can outweigh sampling error. The next step is making that range a default output of evaluation harnesses: a Scorer Card for each task, and audit labels spent where they narrow comparisons most.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can fairness be audited at the decision instead of the metric?",
    text: "Subgroup AUC reads within-group ranking, while a screening threshold acts across groups. Audits should report who a deployed threshold actually flags, at the capacities a programme really runs, with intervals on the gap.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can deployment failure be diagnosed before labels arrive?",
    text: "TrustShift shows that shift magnitude alone does not say which axis fails. The open problem is which label-free probes identify the mechanism, with what guarantees, and how an audit should report inconclusive when they cannot.",
  },
];
---

<section class="future container" id="future">
  <p class="label-mono section-eyebrow" data-reveal>The next five years</p>
  <h2 class="section-title" data-reveal>
    Questions that remain <em>open</em>
  </h2>

  <ol class="future-list">
    {
      questions.map((item, i) => (
        <li class="future-item" data-reveal>
          <span class="label-mono future-index">Q{i + 1}</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="future-q">{item.q}</h3>
            <p class="future-text">{item.text}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>
</section>

<style>
  .future {
    padding-block: var(--space-section);
    border-bottom: var(--rule);
  }

  .section-eyebrow {
    color: var(--signal);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-weight: 460;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .section-title em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .future-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .future-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    border-top: var(--rule);
  }

  .future-index { color: var(--signal); padding-top: 0.5em; }

  .future-q {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .future-text { color: var(--ink-2); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .future-item { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); }
  }
</style>
